.TH BLUETUITH-RS 1 "2026-11-15" "bluetuith-rs 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
bluetuith-rs \- a full-featured Bluetooth manager for the terminal
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B bluetuith-rs
.RI [ OPTIONS ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B bluetuith-rs
is a terminal user interface for managing Bluetooth adapters and devices.
It talks to BlueZ over the system D-Bus and provides adapter control, device
discovery/pairing/connection, OBEX Object Push file send and receive (with an
authorization dialog and a configurable receive directory), AVRCP media
playback, PAN networking and audio profile views. The interface is built with
ratatui and supports the mouse, configurable keybindings, multiple colour
themes and an English/Chinese bilingual UI.
.PP
With
.B \-\-demo
the application runs against a built-in simulated adapter, so it can be used
(and tested) on machines without Bluetooth hardware.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-l ", " \-\-list-adapters
List available adapters and exit.
.TP
.BR \-g ", " \-\-generate
Write a default configuration file and exit.
.TP
.BR \-a ", " \-\-adapter " " \fINAME\fR
Adapter to use (e.g. hci0 or a MAC address).
.TP
.BR \-r ", " \-\-receive-dir " " \fIDIR\fR
Directory for received OBEX files (default ~/Downloads/bluetuith-rs).
.TP
.BR \-m ", " \-\-gsm-apn " " \fIAPN\fR
APN for DUN dial-up networking (reserved; no effect yet).
.TP
.BR \-b ", " \-\-gsm-number " " \fINUMBER\fR
Number to dial for DUN (reserved; no effect yet, default *99#).
.TP
.BR \-s ", " \-\-adapter-states " " \fILIST\fR
Startup states, e.g. 'powered:yes,discoverable:yes,scan:no'.
.TP
.BR \-t ", " \-\-connect-bdaddr " " \fIMAC\fR
Auto-connect this device on startup.
.TP
.BR \-w ", " \-\-no-warning
Suppress startup warnings (keybinding conflicts, reserved options).
.TP
.BR \-i ", " \-\-no-help-display
Hide the bottom keybinding strip.
.TP
.BR \-c ", " \-\-confirm-on-quit
Ask for confirmation before quitting.
.TP
.B "\-\-no-confirm-on-quit"
Quit immediately.
.TP
.BR \-o ", " \-\-disable-obex-services
Disable OBEX file send and receive entirely.
.TP
.B "\-\-show-hidden-files"
Show hidden files in the file picker.
.TP
.B "\-\-scan-on-start"
Start discovery at launch.
.TP
.BR "\-\-theme " \fINAME\fR
Palette: Midnight, Nord, Catppuccin, Dracula, Gruvbox, Tokyo Night,
Rosé Pine, Solarized or Daylight.
.TP
.BR "\-\-accent " \fI#RRGGBB\fR
Override the accent colour.
.TP
.BR "\-\-default-sort " \fIKEY\fR
Name, Address, Rssi, Battery, State or Kind.
.TP
.BR "\-\-lang " \fICODE\fR
UI language: en or zh (default auto-detected from $LANG).
.TP
.BR "\-\-config " \fIPATH\fR
Use an alternate configuration file.
.TP
.B "\-\-demo"
Run against a simulated adapter (no BlueZ required).
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print help.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Print version.
.SH KEYBINDINGS
Navigate with the arrow keys. c connect/disconnect, p pair, t trust,
b block, d remove, o power, s scan, Alt+s discoverable, Alt+p pairable,
a change adapter, f send files, v transfers, m media player, Alt+h hide
player, n network options, Alt+a audio profiles, i device info, / search,
l language, F1/F2/F3/F4 menus, F5 sort, F6 details, F7 theme, F8 log,
F9 about, Ctrl+p command palette, Alt+m menu, ? help, q quit, Ctrl+z
suspend, Ctrl+x cancel, Esc close.
.PP
In the media-player window: Space play/pause, < > previous/next track,
Left/Right seek, + \- volume, ] stop, s shuffle, r repeat.
.PP
Letter keys are case-insensitive (q and Q are the same); every binding can be
overridden in the [keybindings] section of the configuration file.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/bluetuith-rs/config.toml
User configuration.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
Options may also be set through BLUETUITH_RS_* variables (the BLUETUITH_*
forms used by the original bluetuith are accepted as aliases).
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR bluetoothctl (1),
.BR bluetoothd (8)
